    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Christian Yelich** stands as the clear anchor of the Zurich Zebras lineup. With a score of 63.76, **Yelich** benefits significantly from the premium #1 spot in the order (+10%) and a dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) against Roupp. While Roupp presents a moderate test, the leadoff positioning ensures **Yelich** maximized opportunities for Runs, our scarcest commodity. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier is **Carson Benge** (54.69), who utilizes a similar leadoff advantage to offset the matchup against Hancock. Despite a grueling draw against Madden\u2019s 2.31 xERA, **Junior Caminero** (48.89) remains a start-worthy play, as his #4 hole in the lineup provides the RBI potential necessary to keep the offense balanced despite the heavy SP skill penalty.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished at 36.86\u2014the highest of our reserves but still below the Zebras' 40-point floor threshold. While **Meidroth** benefited from a positive park factor, his output was ultimately stifled by an aggressive 19% reduction due to the strength of Ryan on the mound, a testament to our strict adherence to efficiency metrics. **Luke Raley** (44.09) and **Colt Keith** (44.78) round out the starting infield, holding just enough value to clear the floor despite facing decent arms in Warren and Jax. Notably, **Yordan Alvarez** sits at 0.00 today due to the team\u2019s scheduled off-day, limiting our power ceiling. As we monitor the wire for potential speed threats like **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, or **Caleb Durbin** to help close the gap in SB, we continue to bench **Casey Schmitt** and **Dillon Dingler** until their matchups improve against weaker pitching rotations. Keep an eye on the late-day weather reports, though no specific warnings currently jeopardize the projected performance of **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, or **Pedro Ramirez**.",
